      "content": "thanks, that's a decent start and definitely feels more grounded than what i was worried about. the flow is good.\n\nactually, now that i'm reading it back, i'm a bit worried it might be *too* plain. i know i said not to stuff it, but i'm looking at the official fellowship guidelines and they really emphasize \"the integration of complex theoretical frameworks.\" I'm worried that if the automated system doesn't see enough of those heavy-hitting academic terms, it'll just toss my application before a human even sees this level of writing.\n\ncould we try a second version? maybe try to weave in more of those high-level terms (like the ones I mentioned before) but try to keep it natural? i really don't want it to look like a word salad, but i also don't want to be too \"safe\" and lose points on the technical complexity side.",
